  "content": {
    "id": "p70-q25-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": "Find the value(s) of $m$ so that the line $y=mx+1$ is a tangent to the parabola $y=x^2+4x+3$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$m=4\\pm2\\sqrt{2}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}mx+1&=x^2+4x+3\\\\x^2+(4-m)x+2&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nTangency requires one intersection, so $\\Delta=0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(4-m)^2-4(1)(2)&=0\\\\(4-m)^2&=8\\\\4-m&=\\pm2\\sqrt{2}\\\\m&=4\\pm2\\sqrt{2}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
